  "content_body": "Kristin Cohen, DNP, CNM, WHNP-BC\n\nAbout Kristin Cohen, DNP, CNM, WHNP-BC\n\nKristin Cohen, DNP, CNM, WHNP-BC, is a certified nurse midwife and a board certified women’s health nurse practitioner.\n\nAs a midwife and nurse practitioner, Cohen specializes in providing evidence-based, patient-centered care that emphasizes health promotion, shared-decision making, and limiting intervention in natural physiologic processes.\n\nExperience\n\nCohen currently practices in New Jersey, where she cares for people during labor and birth, as well as throughout pregnancy and the postpartum period.\n\nShe also provides gynecological care to people of all ages, including annual exams, health screenings, and contraceptive management.\n\nBefore becoming an advanced practice nurse, Cohen worked for many years as a labor and delivery nurse, as well as in home care and infection prevention.\n\nEducation\n\nCohen received her Doctor of Nursing Practice degree from Rutgers University. She holds a B.S. in biology from University of Mary Washington and a B.S. in nursing from the University of Maryland-Baltimore.\n\nThe educational health content on What To Expect is reviewed by our medical review board and team of experts to be up-to-date and in line with the latest evidence-based medical information and accepted health guidelines, including the medically reviewed What to Expect books by Heidi Murkoff. This educational content is not medical or diagnostic advice. Use of this site is subject to our terms of use and privacy policy. © 2005-2026 Everyday Health, Inc., a Ziff Davis company.\n\nOpens a new window",
